# The generic copy comes back, without a test, where the tested code knows nothing more than the copy: the array and the result no longer go around the loop as parameters, the loop names what the block in front of it has.
# Array.prototype.filter as the library has it takes any receiver. It expects what the first overload of its entry accepts, so it tests once for an array with the built-in names
# and then reads elements, makes the result and stores into it without a lookup. The same body behind no entry expects nothing of `this` and of its parameter
